        "original_id": "631c6915-a353-5681-b651-c3a53843daf3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edward Burne-Jones, William Morris\n- Artworks: The Beguiling of Merlin, Pygmalion and the Image, Pygmalion and Galatea series\n- Movements: Pre-Raphaelite movement\n- Companies: Morris, Marshall, Faulkner & Co.\n- Roles: British artist, designer, founding partner\n\nFacts:\n- Edward Burne-Jones was born on 28 August 1833 and died on 17 June 1898.\n- Edward Burne-Jones was a British artist and designer associated with the later phase of the Pre-Raphaelite movement.\n- Edward Burne-Jones worked closely with William Morris on decorative arts as a founding partner in Morris, Marshall, Faulkner & Co.\n- The Beguiling of Merlin is a painting by Pre-Raphaelite painter Edward Burne-Jones that was created between 1872 and 1877.\n- Pygmalion and the Image is the second series of four oil paintings in the Pygmalion and Galatea series by Edward Burne-Jones, completed between 1875 and 1878.",
